:EPARML.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTLINETH/LINKSPEED'.Link speed (LINKSPEED)
:P.The link speed for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*MIN:EPK.
:PD.The smallest value.
:PT.:PK DEF.*MAX:EPK.
:PD.The largest value.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 8 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTLINETH/THRESHOLD'.Error threshold level (THRESHOLD)
:P.The error threshold level for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*OFF:EPK.
:PD.Off.
:PT.:PK.*MIN:EPK.
:PD.The smallest value.
:PT.:PK.*MAX:EPK.
:PD.The largest value.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *MED.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTLINETH/GENTSTFRM'.Generate test frame (GENTSTFRM)
:P.Whether to generate test frame.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTLINETH/AUT'.Authority (AUT)
:P.The authority the public (users with no private authority and no
group authority) gets to the new object.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CHANGE:EPK.
:PD.Change authority&colon. all data authorities and operational
authority. The object can be used and its contents changed.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All authority&colon. the user can do anything with the object except
change its owner or what secures it.
:PT.:PK.*USE:EPK.
:PD.Use authority&colon. the object can be read and run but not changed.
:PT.:PK.*EXCLUDE:EPK.
:PD.No authority&colon. the object cannot be used.
:PT.:PK.*LIBCRTAUT:EPK.
:PD.The create authority of the library the object is created in (CRTAUT
of the library).
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTLINETH/TEXT'.Text 'description' (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DLTLIND.Delete Line Description (DLTLIND)
:P.Use the Delete Line Description (DLTLIND) command to delete line
descriptions that are varied off.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DLTLIND/LIND'.Line description (LIND)
:P.The line description.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DSPLIND.Display Line Description (DSPLIND)
:P.Use the Display Line Description (DSPLIND) command to show a line
description.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPLIND/LIND'.Line description (LIND)
:P.The line description.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPLIND/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*:EPK.
:PD.The output is shown at the display of an interactive job, and
printed for a batch job.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPLIND/OPTION'.Option (OPTION)
:P.The option for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*BASIC:EPK.
:PD.Basic.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *SWTNWILST, *CTL, *SWTCTLLST, *ACTSWTCTL, *SSAP,
*GRPADR, *FCNADR.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=WRKLIND.Work with Line Descriptions (WRKLIND)
:P.Use the Work with Line Descriptions (WRKLIND) command to list line
descriptions and work with them.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKLIND/LIND'.Line description (LIND)
:P.The line description.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *ASYNC, *BSC, *DDI, *ELAN, *FAX, *FR, *IDLC,
*NET, *PPP, *SDLC, *TDLC, *TRLAN, *WLS, *X25.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
